# Capacitor native projects (android/, ios/) ARE committed to version control
# (standard Capacitor convention) — only their generated/build output is
# ignored. Each native platform ships its own .gitignore (generated by
# `npx cap add <platform>`) that already excludes Gradle/.gradle build
# output, copied web assets, local.properties, CocoaPods Pods/, DerivedData,
# xcuserdata, etc. Do not duplicate those rules here — see android/.gitignore
# (and, once added, ios/.gitignore).

# Firebase Android client config. Google documents this as non-secret (its API
# key is restricted by package name + signing-certificate fingerprint), and
# committing it is common practice — but THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC, and the
# file still discloses the project id, sender id and app id. Ignored by
# default; a leak is not reversible once it is in the history, whereas
# choosing to track it later is trivial.
#
# Not to be confused with the Firebase SERVICE ACCOUNT key, which is a genuine
# secret, belongs under backend/storage/app/firebase/, and must never live in
# this directory tree at all — see docs/push-notifications/HANDOFF.md §8.
android/app/google-services.json

